## Delta findings

1. The four prefix-tag push files (accounts, primary-advantage, storytime, workbooks)
   now hold `--tag=<prefix>-$${BUILD_ID:0:8}`. Cloud Build turns `$$` into one literal
   `$`; bash slices the step env `BUILD_ID=$BUILD_ID` to 8 characters. The submit-time
   rejection risk of the earlier review is closed (PM order 2026-11-07).
2. The tests grew stronger. `assertEscapedTag` (W-11 x4, W-15) requires the escaped
   text, requires the env map, and rejects the unescaped form. F-06 expects the
   escaped form. New F-17 scans all 16 push and traffic files for an unescaped
   `${key}` with an invalid key; it asserts `files_checked=16` before the loop.
   Legitimate `${_...}` substitutions pass; `$${...}` escapes pass.
3. Red r3 partial-repair proof stands: a scratch copy with only the storytime tag
   escaped failed with `invalid_substitutions=3`; the all-escaped copy passed.
4. The plan records the intermediate red state honestly (Green run at 586981581
   EXIT=1 on F-06 until Red r4 09ce375d2). No false claim.

